## Harness design notes (why the text checks changed shape mid-run)

- First leak scan used body.innerText substring matching: false positives from
  generic single-word catalog titles that also live in nav chrome ("Progress",
  "Review", "Words" = the PATH_KIND_NAMES kind word). A line-exact pass still
  collided on the kind word. Final rule: structural check on `data-unit` ids
  against the server-side hidden set computed from the unit_path payload —
  exact, immune to title/chrome collisions, and proven non-vacuous by the
  payload gate above.
- hidden-set math mirrors the frontend contract exactly: bands sorted by
  pathOrderRank (done -> open -> locked) before the tail cutoff (the wire
  order is pack file order — raw-order math silently produced 0 hidden).
- Screenshots survive in this dir; the harness writes result-<tag>.json next
  to them. Navigation errors ride INTO the result (MOBILE-UX-001 rule).
